trong",null,{"children":"Kaivalya"}],"—absolute independence or isolation. It is the realization that the pure consciousness (",["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/what-is-atman","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"Purusha or Atman"}],") is distinctly separate from nature, thoughts, and matter (",["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/what-is-samsara","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"Prakriti"}],")."]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground border-border/50 shadow-sm","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold font-sans text-foreground mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary text-sm","children":"3"}],"The Kleshas (Obstacles)"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground","children":"Patanjali outlines five root causes of human suffering: ignorance of the true self (Avidya), egoism (Asmita), attachment (Raga), aversion (Dvesha), and clinging to life (Abhinivesha)."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground border-border/50 shadow-sm","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold font-sans text-foreground mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary text-sm","children":"4"}],"Ashtanga (Eight Limbs)"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground","children":"The practical path to mastering the mind. These progressive eight steps ensure ethical safety, physical steadiness, energetic balance, and profound meditative focus."}]]}]}]]}]]}]
